Z||000000||lennyb4||06-08-2000||08:38 AM||||There's been something on my mind for a while now. Just out of curiousity whats with the obbsession with primates all about?||||reg||6
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-08-2000||03:05 PM||||My wife and I have always loved 'em! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  They're one of the smartest people (er...animals?) out there.  They are also some of the cutest.  (Don't make fun of me, please.)  I don't know.  Watch some of the gorilla movies and you'll fall in love with them, too.  Try this.  Log onto <A HREF="http://www.koko.com" TARGET=_blank>www.koko.com</A>  and see if you don't come away with some feelings for my friends.  (That's just one of many sites, movies, books, etc that my wife and I frequent.)  Primates make you feel like you're somebody.  They can relate to you.  I love dogs.  I think they make great pets, but they can't interact with you like a primate could.  (No.  We don't have any yet.  Someday! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)  <P>This is a difficult question to answer without revealing more of myself than I really want to.  Go to the above website (kinda sad, though.  Kokos friend died <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">) and watch Mighty Joe Young, Born to be Wild, Buddy, or even Project X.  If you don't even think about shedding a tear or two, you have no feelings.  (Nothing personal)  Even through a movie (Buddy was based on a true story), you can feel a bond with them.  When you watch MJY or Buddy, you can just imagine giving them a big hug or sitting next to them at the dinner table (well...maybe not MJY <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).<P>I've said too much.  I gotta go work on the Grape Ape. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
